Adaptation: Go implementation of the named tool_choice contract for the native
in-kernel planner. When tool_choice resolves to one forced function, its
parameters schema constrains decoding through the native JSON-schema logit
mask, so the call's arguments come from the model under the schema rather
than from text heuristics. The mask covers the {name, arguments} envelope the
native forced-tool prompt already asks for, instead of upstream's bare
parameters schema, and the decoded envelope is lifted into the tool call.
Schemas outside the native mask subset, the forced Write artifact mode and
requests the mask cannot serve keep the prior unmasked path. Multi-tool
"required" (upstream's anyOf array) is not adapted.
